@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves a value using an [RFC 6901 JSON
+Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901). The empty pointer returns the document itself;
+object member names and array indices are separated by `/`, with `~0` and `~1` representing `~` and
+`/` respectively. It throws when a pointer is malformed or does not refer to a value.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+resolvePointer({ services: [{ name: "api" }] }, "/services/0/name");
+// "api"
+```
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
